<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>

<application config:interface="com.top_logic.basic.config.ApplicationConfig$Config"
	xmlns:config="http://www.top-logic.com/ns/config/6.0"
>
	<services>
		<config service-class="com.top_logic.tl.ai.core.provider.LLMService">
			<instance class="com.top_logic.tl.ai.core.provider.LLMService">
				<agent-execution
					default-model="%DEFAULT_MODEL%"
				/>
				<!--
					What every agent run is told about the situation it runs in. The harness composes
					this block once per run and puts it into the system prompt - at the {{environment}}
					placeholder when the prompt names one, at the end otherwise, so every shipped agent
					gets it without an edit.

					Its wording is NOT here. It is the resource tl.ai.environment.template
					(WEB-INF/conf/resources/tl-ai-core.app-messages_*.properties), so that it is
					translated like every other text this product ships and survives an application
					that overrides this service wholesale - which is what an application naming its own
					providers does. Set <template> here only to say something different from what the
					product says.

					Whatever it says, it must not contain anything that changes while a conversation
					runs: the block sits in front of every request of that conversation and one changed
					character invalidates the provider's prompt cache for all of them. That is why the
					date is stated at day granularity and why only stable facts reach {{context}}.
				-->
				<environment/>
				<!--
					What this application knows about the identifiers a model passes to a tool.

					When a tool cannot resolve one, TidDiagnostics says which kind of wrong identifier
					it was - a uuid, a printed object, an unknown type, an id of the wrong shape - so
					that the model corrects itself in one step instead of trying the same string in
					the next tool. Those classes are the same everywhere and need no configuration.

					What needs configuration is the identifier this application's own users speak: an
					order number, a ticket code, a part number. Declare one hint per such code; the
					pattern is matched against the whole identifier, and the explanation continues the
					sentence that begins with the quoted identifier:

					<object-ids>
						<hints>
							<hint pattern="[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*-[0-9]+"
								explanation="is a record code. Search for it with sales__search and use the id from the answer."
							/>
						</hints>
					</object-ids>

					gives the model: 'LEAD-014' is a record code. Search for it with sales__search and
					use the id from the answer.
				-->
				<object-ids/>
				<model-catalog />
			</instance>
		</config>
	</services>
</application>
